<?php
/**
 * The address form — Figma 557:5173.
 *
 * Rendered on its own by Spartrak\CustomerAccount\Controller\Address\Form and
 * injected into the address book's dialog. It is the SAME form the checkout's
 * add-address modal draws; see Spartrak\CustomerAccount\ViewModel\AddressForm
 * for why that one is reshaped by a plugin and this one is a template.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * IT POSTS TO CORE, NOT TO US
 * ===========================================================================
 * `action` is `Magento\Customer\Block\Address\Edit::getSaveUrl()`, i.e. core's
 * own `customer/address/formPost`. So validation, the address repository, the
 * success/error messages and the CSRF form-key check are all Magento's — this
 * feature adds no save path of its own and cannot drift from the one the
 * platform maintains.
 *
 * That also decides the no-JavaScript behaviour: this is a real form with a
 * real action, so it submits and redirects on its own. The dialog is an
 * enhancement over a working page, not the thing that makes it work.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE THREE FIELDS FIGMA DOES NOT DRAW
 * ===========================================================================
 * `country_id` is posted as a hidden field from configuration — one country,
 * so asking would be a question with one answer. `city` and `postcode` are not
 * posted at all: Spartrak_CustomerAddress fills the city from the chosen
 * governorate, and postcode is optional for Egypt (its config.xml widens
 * general/country/optional_zip_countries). Omitting country_id as well would
 * produce an address Magento's own validator rejects, from a form with no
 * field to fix it in.
 *
 * THE CITY IS FILLED BY A REPOSITORY PLUGIN, NOT BY THE SAVE-BEFORE OBSERVER.
 * This form posts to core's `customer/address/formPost`, which goes through
 * AddressRepositoryInterface::save() — and that method VALIDATES before it
 * saves, so `customer_address_save_before` fires after the "city is required"
 * rejection, not before it. That is why saving from here used to fail and
 * bounce to /customer/address/edit/. See
 * Spartrak\CustomerAddress\Plugin\FillCityOnAddressRepositorySave.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE FIELD PRIMITIVES ARE THE ACCOUNT SECTION'S OWN
 * ===========================================================================
 * `.spartrak-account-field` already renders a 21px label, a 6px gap and a 48px
 * bordered band — which is, to the pixel, what 557:10372 specifies here. So
 * this form reuses that component rather than defining a second set of inputs
 * that would have to be kept in step with it (CLAUDE.md section 9). Only the
 * two shapes this form introduces are new: the 120px textarea band and the
 * select.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Customer\Block\Address\Edit $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */

use Spartrak\CustomerAccount\ViewModel\AddressForm;

/** @var AddressForm|null $addressForm */
$addressForm = $block->getData('address_form');
$address = $block->getAddress();
$addressId = (int) $address->getId();
$isNew = $addressId === 0;

$governorates = $addressForm !== null ? $addressForm->getGovernorateOptions() : [];
$selectedRegion = (string) ($address->getRegionId() ?? '');
$streetText = $addressForm !== null ? $addressForm->getStreetText($address) : '';
$additionalPhone = $addressForm !== null ? $addressForm->getAdditionalPhone($address) : '';
$isDefault = $addressForm !== null && $addressForm->isDefault($address);
?>
<?php /*
  `novalidate` + `data-mage-init="validation"` is Magento's own pairing: the
  browser's native bubbles are switched off so the platform's widget owns the
  messages, which is what renders them inline in the styles this theme already
  has.

  THE WIDGET WAS NEVER TURNED ON BEFORE. Measured on the deployed store: this
  fragment carried no `data-mage-init` at all, so every `required` and every
  `data-validate` below was decoration — with native validation suppressed by
  `novalidate` and nothing else listening, an empty required field submitted,
  and the shopper got a server round trip and a redirect instead of an inline
  message.

  ONE DECLARATION, BOTH RENDERS. Magento scans for `data-mage-init` once at
  page load, which covers the standalone render (Controller\Address\Form's own
  route, and the no-JavaScript path). The dialog injects this markup afterwards,
  by AJAX, so js/address-dialog.js re-runs that same initialiser over the
  fragment — it reads this attribute rather than naming the widget again in
  JavaScript, so the rules live here and only here.
*/ ?>
<form class="spartrak-address-form"
      action="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getSaveUrl()) ?>"
      method="post"
      id="spartrak-address-form"
      data-spartrak-address-form
      data-mage-init='{"validation":{}}'
      novalidate>
    <?= $block->getBlockHtml('formkey') ?>

    <?php if (!$isNew) : ?>
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="<?= (int) $addressId ?>">
    <?php endif; ?>

    <?php /* Configuration, not a question. See the header. */ ?>
    <input type="hidden"
           name="country_id"
           value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($addressForm?->getCountryId() ?? '') ?>">

    <div class="spartrak-address-form__grid">
        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-firstname">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('First name')) ?>
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band">
                <input type="text"
                       class="spartrak-account-field__input"
                       id="spartrak-address-firstname"
                       name="firstname"
                       value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($address->getFirstname() ?? '') ?>"
                       placeholder="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Please enter your first name')) ?>"
                       autocomplete="given-name"
                       required
                       data-validate="{'required':true}">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-lastname">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Last name')) ?>
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band">
                <input type="text"
                       class="spartrak-account-field__input"
                       id="spartrak-address-lastname"
                       name="lastname"
                       value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($address->getLastname() ?? '') ?>"
                       placeholder="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Please enter your last name')) ?>"
                       autocomplete="family-name"
                       required
                       data-validate="{'required':true}">
            </div>
        </div>

        <?php /*
          Full width (557:10340). A real <select> rather than a scripted list:
          it is a single choice from a fixed set, which is what the element is
          for — the design's chevron is drawn on the band by the stylesheet and
          the native control keeps keyboard, screen-reader and mobile-wheel
          behaviour for free (CLAUDE.md: native behaviour over JavaScript).
        */ ?>
        <div class="spartrak-account-field spartrak-address-form__field--wide">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-region">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Governorate')) ?>
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band spartrak-account-field__band--select">
                <select class="spartrak-account-field__select"
                        id="spartrak-address-region"
                        name="region_id"
                        required
                        data-validate="{'required':true}">
                    <option value=""><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Choose a region or governorate')) ?></option>
                    <?php foreach ($governorates as $option) : ?>
                        <option value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($option['value']) ?>"
                            <?= $option['value'] === $selectedRegion ? ' selected' : '' ?>>
                            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($option['label']) ?>
                        </option>
                    <?php endforeach; ?>
                </select>
            </div>
        </div>

        <?php /*
          ONE textarea for the whole address (721:29509, 120px tall), where
          Magento stores street as an ordered list of lines. Posted as
          `street[0]`, and read back joined on newlines by
          AddressForm::getStreetText() — so a two-line address written by an
          admin or the API survives a save from here instead of losing every
          line but the first.
        */ ?>
        <div class="spartrak-account-field spartrak-address-form__field--wide">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-street">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Address details')) ?>
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band spartrak-account-field__band--textarea">
                <textarea class="spartrak-account-field__input spartrak-account-field__input--textarea"
                          id="spartrak-address-street"
                          name="street[0]"
                          rows="4"
                          placeholder="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Please write your address in full')) ?>"
                          required
                          data-validate="{'required':true}"><?= $escaper->escapeHtml($streetText) ?></textarea>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-telephone">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Mobile number')) ?>
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band">
                <input type="tel"
                       class="spartrak-account-field__input"
                       id="spartrak-address-telephone"
                       name="telephone"
                       value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($address->getTelephone() ?? '') ?>"
                       placeholder="01xxxxxxxxxx"
                       autocomplete="tel"
                       dir="ltr"
                       required
                       data-validate="{'required':true}">
            </div>
        </div>

        <?php /*
          The one optional field in the form — no asterisk, and no `required`.
          A custom attribute (Spartrak_CustomerAddress's AddAdditionalPhoneAttribute
          patch), which is why its value is read through the custom-attribute bag
          rather than a getter.

          OPTIONAL, BUT NOT UNCHECKED. When a value IS given it has to be a real
          Egyptian mobile number, enforced by
          Spartrak\CustomerAddress\Model\Validator\AdditionalPhone on Magento's
          own address-validator composite — so it holds for this form, for the
          checkout's modal, for the admin customer form and for the REST API
          alike. Until that class existed the field accepted any 32 characters:
          a name, an email, half a sentence.

          NO `data-validate` FORMAT RULE HERE, deliberately. The rule is
          Spartrak_CustomerAuth's Phone\Normalizer — the store's single
          definition of a usable mobile number, shared with sign-up and sign-in.
          It folds Arabic-Indic and Persian digits, accepts `01…`, `+20…` and
          `0020…`, and then requires a reachable NSN. A hand-written regex in
          this attribute could not do the digit folding without becoming
          unreadable, and one that got it wrong would reject the Arabic keyboard
          this store's primary locale is typed on. So the format is checked in
          the one place that already knows the answer, and the message comes
          back naming the field with an example.
        */ ?>
        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <label class="spartrak-account-field__label" for="spartrak-address-additional-phone">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Additional number')) ?>
            </label>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band">
                <input type="tel"
                       class="spartrak-account-field__input"
                       id="spartrak-address-additional-phone"
                       name="additional_phone"
                       value="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($additionalPhone) ?>"
                       placeholder="01xxxxxxxxxx"
                       dir="ltr">
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <?php /*
      "العنوان الافتراضي" (557:10445) — ONE control where Magento keeps two
      defaults, so it posts both.

      The mirror is a second real checkbox, visually hidden and kept in step by
      the dialog's script. Without JavaScript only the SHIPPING default is set,
      which is the honest degradation for a shipping address book — the shopper
      still gets the default they asked for on the axis this storefront
      actually uses. See Controller\Address\SetDefault for why the two flags are
      never allowed to diverge deliberately.
    */ ?>
    <div class="spartrak-address-form__default">
        <label class="spartrak-address-form__toggle" for="spartrak-address-default">
            <span class="spartrak-address-form__toggle-label">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Default address')) ?>
            </span>
            <input type="checkbox"
                   class="spartrak-address-form__toggle-input"
                   id="spartrak-address-default"
                   name="default_shipping"
                   value="1"
                   data-spartrak-address-default
                <?= $isDefault ? ' checked' : '' ?>>
            <span class="spartrak-address-form__toggle-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </label>
        <input type="checkbox"
               class="spartrak-visually-hidden"
               name="default_billing"
               value="1"
               tabindex="-1"
               aria-hidden="true"
               data-spartrak-address-default-mirror
            <?= $isDefault ? ' checked' : '' ?>>
    </div>

    <div class="spartrak-address-form__actions">
        <button type="submit" class="spartrak-address-form__save">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($isNew ? __('Add a new address') : __('Save address')) ?>
        </button>
        <?php /*
          "تجاهل" — AN ANCHOR, AND IT HAS TO BE ONE.

          This template renders in two places: inside the address book's dialog,
          and as a page at /customer/address/new|edit (see
          Magento_Customer/layout/customer_address_form.xml for the four ways
          that page is reached). A <button type="button"> is inert on the page —
          it was a dead control there, with nothing to cancel to.

          One element serves both. In the dialog, js/address-dialog binds
          `[data-spartrak-address-cancel]` on the dialog host, calls
          preventDefault() and closes the modal, so the href is never followed.
          On the page the form is not inside that host, no handler exists, and
          the link simply goes back to the address book — which is also the
          behaviour a shopper with no JavaScript gets in either place.

          The address book rather than Address\Edit::getBackUrl(): that method
          answers `customer/account` when the customer has no addresses yet,
          which was correct while an empty book redirected away and is wrong now
          that it renders (Plugin\Customer\ShowEmptyAddressBook). "تجاهل" means
          "take me back to my addresses" on both paths.
        */ ?>
        <a class="spartrak-address-form__cancel"
           href="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getUrl('customer/address')) ?>"
           data-spartrak-address-cancel>
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Discard')) ?>
        </a>
    </div>
</form>
